     Suppose that the input function f is strictly Kν -periodic. Then, by Lemma 5, the
state |Ψν−1 i just prior the test Testν is at most at a distance ǫ = 22r s/2 away from the

initial state |Ψinit i. Thus the probability that test Testν fails in producing the correct
